    {
      "id": "e11",
      "name": "TextBox 10",
      "hidden": false,
      "parentId": null,
      "inheritedFrom": null,
      "kind": "shape",
      "text": "The Bank has an established Strategic Risk Management Framework (SRMF) that integrates inter-related enterprise-wide processes to manage and oversee strategic risk. \nThe SRMF requires the First Line to ensure regulatory capital consumption and growth in Risk Weighted Assets (RWAs) is supported by adequate revenue and profit generation. \nThe Bank’s Strategic Planning incorporates Capital and Financial planning including key capital metrics and constraints. Global Risk Management (GRM) Senior Management, challenges the Bank’s Business Strategies and Plans considering the Bank’s strategic and financial priorities, and established Risk Appetite Metrics. \nGRM monitors the Bank’s execution of its strategy, horizon scan of emerging threats, and business environment via the Top & Emerging Risk Assessment process. This enables the development of an independent second line view of the Bank’s Strategic Risk Profile. \nGRM monitors the following risk metrics to oversee the Business’ capital consumption and revenue/profit generation as part of its monitoring activities: \nRoE, RoRWA, RAM (Enterprise Risk Appetite Metrics)1\nStrategic KPIs (KPIs pertaining to the four pillars of the Bank’s strategy)\nNIAT and PTPP v/s Plan2 \nRoRWA and RWA growth v/s Plan\nThe Bank’s Strategic Risk Profile is reported to the Bank’s Risk Management Committee (RMC) and the Risk Committee of the Board on a quarterly basis via the Quarterly Risk Report (QRR).  ",
      "placeholder": null,
      "typography": {
        "paragraphs": [
